Decider answers when it is confident; Opus answers the rest
Decider v1.1 on the 2,198 questions. We replayed recorded answers.

                         ┌─────────────┐
                         │  Question   │
                         └──────┬──────┘
                                ▼
                        ┌───────────────┐
                        │ Decider v1.1  │  about 0.23 s per question
                        └───────┬───────┘
                                ▼
          ┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐
          │     Among its most confident quarter?     │
          └─────┬───────────────────────────────┬─────┘
            Yes │                               │ No
                ▼                               ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────┐    ┌────────────────────────────┐
  │         We keep          │    │  Claude Opus 5.5 answers,  │
  │     Decider's answer     │    │  and we use Opus's answer  │
  └──────────────────────────┘    └────────────────────────────┘

        25% of questions                 75% of questions
        546 of 550 right              about 13 s per request
                                         of 16 questions

The same steps work with Claude Sonnet 5.5, GPT-6 Astra, GPT-6.1 Sol
and Gemini 3.8 Flash.
